{"name":"Silent Storm","hex":"#c3c7bd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silent","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Free from sound or noise; absolutely still; perfectly quiet.","Not speaking; indisposed to talk; speechless; mute; taciturn; not loquacious; not talkative."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["That which is silent; a time of silence.","A silent movie"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silent"},{"term":"storm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any disturbed state of the atmosphere causing destructive or unpleasant weather, especially one affecting the earth's surface involving strong winds (leading to high waves at sea) and usually lightning, thunder, and precipitation.","A heavy fall of precipitation (hail, rain, or snow) or bout of lightning and thunder without strong winds; a hail storm, rainstorm, snowstorm, or thunderstorm."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Preceded by the dummy subject it: to have strong winds and usually lightning and thunder, and/or hail, rain, or snow.","To make (someone or something) stormy; to agitate (someone or something) violently.\n\n\nTo disturb or trouble (someone)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/storm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silent Storm","blocks":[{"text":"Silent Storm is a 2003 turn-based tactics video game developed by Nival Interactive and published by JoWooD. The game is set in a fictionalized World War II Europe with science fiction elements."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b2/SilentStormBox.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silent_Storm","wikidata":"Q2632743"},{"title":"Silent Storm (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Silent Storm\" is a song by Norwegian singer and songwriter Carl Espen, released as the debut single on 18 February 2014. Described as a powerful ballad about finding one's place in life, it was written by Josefin Winther and produced by Magnus Skylstad. The song represented Norway in the Eurovision Song Contest 2014 in Copenhagen, Denmark after winning Melodi Grand Prix 2014, Norway's national selection for the event. The song finished eighth overall with 88 points."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/02/Silent-Storm-Carl-Espen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silent_Storm_(song)","wikidata":"Q15948804"},{"title":"Storm","blocks":[{"text":"A storm is any disturbed state of the natural environment or the atmosphere of an astronomical body. It may be marked by significant disruptions to normal conditions such as strong wind, tornadoes, hail, thunder and lightning, heavy precipitation, heavy freezing rain, strong winds, wind transporting some substance through the atmosphere such as in a dust storm, among other forms of severe weather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Cloud_cumulonimbus_at_baltic_sea%281%29.jpg/330px-Cloud_cumulonimbus_at_baltic_sea%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Storm","wikidata":"Q81054"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/41/Silent_Storm_pose.JPG/330px-Silent_Storm_pose.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/41/Silent_Storm_pose.JPG/330px-Silent_Storm_pose.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An in-game screenshot showing troops and Panzerkleins","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilent_Storm_pose.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/ESC2014_-_Norway_01.jpg/500px-ESC2014_-_Norway_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/